# npm run-* always spawns a shell. On some Windows hosts (notably Cursor
# PowerShell), ComSpec is unset, so npm fails immediately with:
#   ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE: The "file" argument must be of type string. Received undefined
# Pin the Windows script shell so `npm run dev` can start Vite.
# Linux CI clears this key before npm scripts (see .github/workflows/frontend.yml).
script-shell=C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe
